+//! Disruption budgets: how many pods a drain may take, and the one that takes none.
+//!
+//! A PodDisruptionBudget is the promise a cluster keeps to a workload during *voluntary* work —
+//! node drains, upgrades. `minAvailable` and `maxUnavailable` are two spellings of the same number,
+//! and the interesting cases are the edges: a budget of zero allowed evictions is a workload that
+//! blocks every drain (an alert, not a safety feature), and a budget larger than the workload
+//! cannot create pods that are not there.
+//!
+//! ## What you write
+//!
+//! [`allowed`] — how many pods may be evicted at once: `replicas - minAvailable` for the first
+//! spelling, `maxUnavailable` for the second, both capped at `replicas` and never below zero.
+
+/// One of the two spellings of a disruption budget.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+pub enum Budget {
+    /// At least this many pods stay up.
+    MinAvailable(u32),
+    /// At most this many pods go down.
+    MaxUnavailable(u32),
+}
+
+/// How many pods may be evicted at once.
+#[must_use]
+pub fn allowed(replicas: u32, budget: Budget) -> u32 {
+    todo!("both spellings, capped at the replicas, never below zero")
+}
